      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "TULHURST ELVIS (1) drew a wide gate last start and was safely held, beaten 9 metres into seventh at Bathurst over 1730m. Has the benefit of a far better draw. This should be an easier assignment so he is a major player. ZACHARY SHANNON (6) recorded a strong performance last time when he battled on bravely to just miss out over 1730m at Bathurst. Won't find this any harder and he can take this out. CHAMPAGNE WALSH (7) missed the placings two runs back then did a great job to score by 2 metres despite breaking in the run over 1730m at Bathurst four days ago. Drawn to enjoy a cosy run but might need things to go his way at some stage. Meets a similar line up so he must be considered. BIZZIE LIZZIE (3) is the best of the rest after finishing sixth over 1730m at Bathurst last time out.",
